{"cut_proposal":{"candidate_errors":[],"prefix":"To solve the problem, we need to determine the range of positive integers that have four digits in base 3 and two digits in base 6, and then find the average of these integers.\n\n### Step 1: Determine the range of integers for four digits in base 3\nA four-digit number in base 3 can be written as \\( \\overline{abcd}_3 \\), where \\( a, b, c, \\) and \\( d \\) are digits in base 3 (i.e., \\( 0, 1, \\) or \\( 2 \\)), and \\( a \\neq 0 \\). The smallest four-digit number in base 3 is \\( 1000_3 \\) and the largest is \\( 2222_3 \\).\n\nConverting these to base 10:\n- \\( 1000_3 = 1 \\cdot 3^3 + 0 \\cdot 3^2 + 0 \\cdot 3^1 + 0 \\cdot 3^0 = 27 \\)\n- \\( 2222_3 = 2 \\cdot 3^3 + 2 \\cdot 3^2 + 2 \\cdot 3^1 + 2 \\cdot 3^0 = 2 \\cdot (27 + 9 + 3 + 1) = 2 \\cdot 40 = 80 \\)\n\nSo, the range of integers in base 10 that have four digits in base 3 is from 27 to 80.\n\n### Step 2: Determine the range of integers for two digits in base 6\nA two-digit number in base 6 can be written as \\( \\overline{ab}_6 \\), where \\( a \\) and \\( b \\) are digits in base 6 (i.e., \\( 0, 1, 2, 3, 4, \\) or \\( 5 \\)), and \\( a \\neq 0 \\). The smallest two-digit number in base 6 is \\( 10_6 \\) and the largest is \\( 55_6 \\).\n\n","prefix_end":1161,"status":"review_required"},"eligible":false,"generation":{"generation":{"max_new_tokens":2048,"temperature":0.7,"top_k":0,"top_p":1.0},"ids":[1249,11625,279,3491,11,582,1184,311,8253,279,2088,315,6785,25780,429,614,3040,18509,304,2331,220,18,323,1378,18509,304,2331,220,21,11,323,1221,1477,279,5461,315,1493,25780,382,14374,14822,220,16,25,29901,279,2088,315,25780,369,3040,18509,304,2331,220,18,198,32,3040,48342,1372,304,2331,220,18,646,387,5326,438,17767,1124,1975,1056,90,68644,19444,18,1124,701,1380,17767,264,11,293,11,272,11,1124,8,323,17767,294,1124,8,525,18509,304,2331,220,18,320,72,1734,2572,17767,220,15,11,220,16,11,1124,8,476,17767,220,17,1124,5731,323,17767,264,1124,811,80,220,15,1124,568,